1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:03,750
This is Cantá, in Roraima, in the
Brazilian Amazon.

2
00:00:03,790 --> 00:00:05,840
Rosa just pulled up her cassava.

3
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:08,910
And after every harvest, she asks the same
question…

4
00:00:08,950 --> 00:00:10,410
What do I plant next?

5
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:12,560
AgroDeal helps her answer it.

6
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,900
The name says deal, but it sells nothing.

7
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:17,440
It lets the farmer choose what to
optimize.

8
00:00:17,710 --> 00:00:20,460
First, the problem, measured with NASA
POWER.

9
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:25,050
From June to September, Cantá got three
hundred and thirty millimeters of rain.

10
00:00:25,090 --> 00:00:30,120
The average is eight hundred and fifty-
nine. The lowest since 1981.

11
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:34,880
The longest dry spell in the rainy season:
twenty-four days. Normally, nine.

12
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:39,560
By September, the soil was as dry as in
January. Five months early.

13
00:00:39,830 --> 00:00:42,050
Will 2027 repeat it?

14
00:00:42,090 --> 00:00:47,950
In El Niño years, that rain ranged from forty-eight
percent below average, to seventeen above.

15
00:00:47,990 --> 00:00:51,190
There is no rule. So we don't predict. We
observe.

16
00:00:51,460 --> 00:00:52,690
Second, the people.

17
00:00:52,730 --> 00:00:58,280
In the last census, eighty-seven percent of
Roraima's farms had no technical assistance.

18
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:03,730
Right now, the state extension agency tells families
to choose crops suited to the dry period…

19
00:01:03,770 --> 00:01:06,740
but it only reaches as far as an agent can
drive.

20
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:10,540
In our survey, most families plant again
right after harvest.

21
00:01:10,580 --> 00:01:14,310
And a farmer in Goiás told us many were
afraid to invest.

22
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:15,640
Tools exist.

23
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:20,090
Brazil's official zoning tells you when to
plant the crop you already chose.

24
00:01:20,130 --> 00:01:26,620
And a peer-reviewed study found that almost all rotation
tools optimize only profit, for big farms.

25
00:01:26,660 --> 00:01:31,040
None we found starts from the harvest, and
lets the small farmer pick the goal.

26
00:01:31,310 --> 00:01:32,660
So, back to Rosa.

27
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:38,590
Better soil? Cowpea. It's not related to cassava, so
the pest left in the ground won't take it.

28
00:01:38,630 --> 00:01:44,260
Low risk, in July? Cowpea again, for another
reason. Out of the ground in seventy days.

29
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:50,700
July is inside the official cowpea window, so the fit
jumps from fifty-three to eighty-seven percent.

30
00:01:50,740 --> 00:01:55,430
Ask for pasture: brachiaria. But it admits it
doesn't know how long it takes.

31
00:01:55,470 --> 00:01:58,310
Ask about income: it says it can't measure
that.

32
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:01,360
Every option gets three numbers. Never
mixed.

33
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:05,260
Risk: from NASA rain and soil moisture,
adjusted to this year.

34
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:07,790
Fit: from crop traits, weighed by her
choice.

35
00:02:07,830 --> 00:02:10,670
And confidence: how much we could actually
measure.

36
00:02:10,710 --> 00:02:15,600
Plain arithmetic on named data, in the
browser. No model guesses a number.

37
00:02:15,870 --> 00:02:18,290
Same maize, same code, two places.

38
00:02:18,330 --> 00:02:24,480
Cantá, in April: six hundred and eighty-six
millimeters, against five hundred needed. Low risk.

39
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:28,770
Rio Verde, in September: three hundred and
eighty-six. High risk.

40
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:34,380
What it can't do, it says. No rain forecast.
No prices. Fourteen crops, so far.

41
00:02:34,420 --> 00:02:38,600
Next: more official windows, field tests
in Roraima, and WhatsApp.

42
00:02:38,870 --> 00:02:41,190
AgroDeal won't tell Rosa what to do.

43
00:02:41,230 --> 00:02:44,000
It shows what each choice does to her
soil, this year.

44
00:02:44,070 --> 00:02:45,410
What do I plant next?

45
00:02:45,450 --> 00:02:47,130
Now, she can explore it.
